  "details": "I’ve seen that this is a hot topic on VR Chat but I’m here to also support the movement and give my perspective as a point of view.\n\nI for one do not mind playing with all ages if I go to a room / instance intended for all ages. However, i do feel like there needs to be safe areas away from underaged individuals that aren’t as fool proof as clicking a sign that doesn’t check anything and allows you to enter regardless. \n\nThere is a popular instance called “drinking game” that has remained on trending places for quite some time and it does require you to read their list of rules - one of them including, “By clicking this I agree that I am at least 18 years of age.” And that allows you to enter the room(s) available. However, there’s no real way to have some sort of vetting process because there’s at least 200 odd something people in various instances. There have definitely been children as young as 6 in these places.\n\nWhen I play VR chat there are (moreover than not) moments where I just want to have a conversation or play a game with someone that is over 18 and doesn’t screech in my ear or require the entire room‘s attention. To be able to talk and have jokes about 18+ things without having to worry about the ears of little ones listening in. \n\nI for one would not mind sending in a photo ID and / or paying for a badge that not only allows me to enter instances / events that are 18+ and have on my profile that I am verified to be 18+.\n\nAs a person with two nephews and that have accessibility to VR chat, I do play with them on private instances that are made for all ages and I do believe that they have a place in VR chat, just certainly not in 18+ worlds that are easy to bypass their rules without any vetting process. \n\nI also believe this would crack down on those who seek younger individuals to be companions in the sense of a relationship or whatever it may be. Although we very well know and can mostly tell what age someone is from their voice and actions, this would prove to those who unfortunately seek out underage companions and as a community we could all see what the big idea is here, and report individuals for grooming if they are claiming to be in sort of situation that is not only socially frowned upon, but straight up illegal.\n\nI’ve spoken to many people in VR chat about this issue, and not one adult has had an issue with the idea of providing their ID to prove their age. \n\nI do not think this should be tacked on as a monthly fee. It should be a one time verification of sending in, faxing, or emailing a scanned copy of your photo ID and if absolutely needed, a CHEAP and affordable purchase of the age approved badge. \n\nWith this, room ratings should be created and show up in peoples’ feeds for trending etc based on their status.\n\nI hope this is looked into and taken very seriously. I’ve experienced too many instances where I’ve witnessed children being in bars and instances where they shouldn’t be - that require you to read the rules and click, “I am 18+” and just the sound of their voice you can absolutely tell that they are off in age by at least another 10 years.\n\nI feel like this would help improve VR Chat immensely and cut down on people who have sick ideologies, preventing more schandals for VR chat, and appeal to the adults who would like to have fun without dealing with underaged individuals.",
